+config NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_IDLETIMER_NL_MSG
+	bool "IDLETIMER send_nl_msg support (Android)"
+	depends on NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_IDLETIMER
+	help
+	  This option lets the `IDLETIMER' target take `--send_nl_msg'. A
+	  timer that has it also sends a uevent with its interface, its state
+	  (active or inactive), the boot time of the change in nanoseconds and,
+	  when it wakes up, the user ID that sent the packet, so a daemon can
+	  track when an interface goes idle. Every timer also restarts as
+	  Android's netd expects it, and a timer that expires while the system
+	  is suspended is corrected on resume.
+
+	  Without it `--send_nl_msg' is refused with EOPNOTSUPP, as upstream
+	  does. If unsure, say N.
